{"parentUuid":"aaef62ea-24d7-448b-bcb3-d3744426bae5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A3QjyACwesEhDbXjJnbZAz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Laurent Perron CP-SAT industrial production deployment talk Google\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Laurent PERRON | Tech Lead Operations Research | PhD Computer Science | Google Inc., Mountain View | Google | Research Department | Research profile\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Laurent-Perron-2\"},{\"title\":\"Laurent Perron\",\"url\":\"https://research.google/people/105821/\"},{\"title\":\"[Scheduling seminar] Laurent Perron (Google France) | The CP-SAT solver - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vvUxusrUcpU\"},{\"title\":\"Laurent Perron\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=umrglaIAAAAJ&hl=en\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: Laurent Perron\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/pid/73/4963.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"The CP-SAT-LP Solver (Invited Talk) - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3\"},{\"title\":\"Monitor search in CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/r54A2eokoXk\"},{\"title\":\"lperron (Laurent Perron) · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lperron\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about Laurent Perron and CP-SAT. Based on the search results:\n\nLaurent Perron is working on Operations Research, with his contributions visible in the OR-Tools package. OR-Tools contains several solvers, including CP-SAT (a gold-medal winner at several MiniZinc competitions, developed since 2009).\n\nThe search results also show that the CP-SAT-LP solver is developed by the Operations Research team at Google and is an implementation of a constraint programming solver on top of a SAT solver using Lazy Clause Generation.\n\nRegarding industrial deployment, the routing component focuses on solving large-scale industrial vehicle-routing problems with complex constraints.\n\nThere is also evidence of talk presentations by Laurent Perron on CP-SAT - I found a YouTube video titled \"[Scheduling seminar] Laurent Perron (Google France) | The CP-SAT solver\" from March 2024, though the search results don't provide complete details about a specific talk on industrial production deployment.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"298f654e-d1f8-4432-9800-bf7ae05d650f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:04.987Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aaef62ea-24d7-448b-bcb3-d3744426bae5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9931c982-4d12-466a-a830-10210dced04b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q9QFgYVKfBFs8EWvpKYKpQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Stitch Fix CP-SAT OR-Tools production constraint programming\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Rostering: Complete Guide to Constraint Programming for Workforce Scheduling - Interactive | Michael Brenndoerfer | Michael Brenndoerfer\",\"url\":\"https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/cp-sat-rostering-constraint-programming-workforce-scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Optimization | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Constraint Programming Solver | google/or-tools | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/google/or-tools/4.1-cp-sat-constraint-programming-solver\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"},{\"title\":\"Kinda Technical | A Guide to Constraint Programming - CP-SAT Solver in OR-Tools\",\"url\":\"https://kindatechnical.com/constraint-programming/lesson-28-cp-sat-solver-in-or-tools.html\"},{\"title\":\"How to modify variables and constraints of an existing CP-model\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/tHUYwwgKYbQ\"}]\n\nI found search results about CP-SAT and OR-Tools, but they don't contain specific information about Stitch Fix using these technologies. Let me provide you with what the search revealed about CP-SAT and OR-Tools:\n\n## CP-SAT and OR-Tools Overview\n\nCP-SAT (Constraint Programming - Satisfiability) is Google OR-Tools' constraint programming solver that combines the expressiveness of constraint programming with the efficiency of modern SAT (Boolean Satisfiability) solvers.\n\nThe CP-SAT Solver is a core component of Google OR-Tools that combines constraint programming (CP) techniques with Boolean satisfiability (SAT) solving technology. This hybrid approach enables efficient solutions for constraint satisfaction and optimization problems across various domains.\n\n## Applications\n\nCP-SAT is well-suited for employee scheduling, where companies that operate continuously need to create weekly schedules. It's used in employee scheduling, where numerous constraints, such as shifts and days off, reduce the number of viable schedules. The relatively new CP-SAT of Google's OR-Tools suite shows to overcome many of the weaknesses and provides a viable alternative to MIP-solvers, being competitive for many problems and sometimes even superior.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain any specific information about Stitch Fix's use of CP-SAT or OR-Tools for production constraint programming. If you're looking for information about how Stitch Fix specifically uses these tools, you may need to search for their technical blog posts, engineering documentation, or conference talks.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c8e0f6ea-2054-4009-9b7a-a2b1012a9d72","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:06.602Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9931c982-4d12-466a-a830-10210dced04b","userType":"external","entrypo