{"parentUuid":"27acd7a3-dfa9-41ad-bcd7-ff5f4b5077b9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XfvKudnkFG8rjrAmwkbFcs","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DoorDash Uber Spotify OR-Tools CP-SAT engineering blog production\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"How Uber & DoorDash empower developers to preview every code change in production\",\"url\":\"https://www.signadot.com/blog/how-uber-and-doordash-enable-developers-to-test-in-production/\"},{\"title\":\"Spotify’s official technology blog | Spotify Engineering\",\"url\":\"https://engineering.atspotify.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Engineering Blog - DoorDash\",\"url\":\"https://careersatdoordash.com/engineering-blog/\"},{\"title\":\"MLOps Community on X: \\\"I can't stop thinking about the evolution of Uber's Michelangelo post. Since getting into the ML space I thought big companies were so advanced. Reading the engineering blogs of Spotify, Uber, Doordash, Pinterest and Airbnb made me feel like they have it all figured out. In https://t.co/VchgvBEPEh\\\" / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/mlopscommunity/status/1802738774352273664\"},{\"title\":\"Engineering | Uber Blog\",\"url\":\"https://eng.uber.com/\"},{\"title\":\"ChatGPT App Integrations Explained: Spotify, DoorDash, Uber, Canva, and More - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vm_gwg1q1rI\"},{\"title\":\"engineering-blogs/engineering_blogs.opml at master · kilimchoi/engineering-blogs\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/kilimchoi/engineering-blogs/blob/master/engineering_blogs.opml\"},{\"title\":\"DoorDash Engineering Blog (@DoorDashEng) / Posts / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/DoorDashEng\"},{\"title\":\"DoorDash’s AI Strategy: Analysis of Dominance in Delivery Commerce AI - Klover.ai\",\"url\":\"https://www.klover.ai/doordash-ai-strategy-analysis-of-dominance-in-delivery-commerce-ai/\"},{\"title\":\"Developer productivity with Dr. Nicole Forsgren (the creator of DORA)\",\"url\":\"https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com/p/developer-productivity-with-dr-nicole\"}]\n\nI found search results related to DoorDash, Uber, and Spotify engineering blogs, though the results don't specifically mention OR-Tools CP-SAT. Here's what I found:\n\n**Engineering Blogs:**\n- Spotify's official technology blog features stories about how they build, covering AI, mobile, web, data science, experimentation, developer tools, design, and open source.\n- DoorDash and Uber both maintain engineering blogs with various technical content.\n\n**Production Testing at DoorDash & Uber:**\nUber developed SLATE (Short-Lived Application Testing Environment) to create on-demand ephemeral testing environments, while DoorDash adopted a new approach to preview features in the production Kubernetes environment.\n\n**AI/ML Work:**\nDoorDash's engineering materials suggest they have a platform called MLW (Machine Learning Warehouse), which lacks the scale and ambition compared to Uber's Michelangelo.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about OR-Tools CP-SAT usage by these companies. If you're looking for specific content about their use of Google's OR-Tools constraint programming solver, you may want to search their engineering blogs directly or refine your search query.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ae207134-f115-440c-b9ee-88413d57e4b5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:07.393Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"27acd7a3-dfa9-41ad-bcd7-ff5f4b5077b9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"20e3b46c-36de-4752-ad97-7bcb288259f3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FqceJN4n5hhU9N92Tv57Mg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"CP-SAT\" production case study company deployment placement layout 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ExCoS @ CP/SAT 2025\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/excos2025\"},{\"title\":\"SaT-CPS 2024\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/sat-cps-2024/\"},{\"title\":\"cp-sat · GitHub Topics · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/topics/cp-sat\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"The SAT Competition - CP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/competitions.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Rostering: Complete Guide to Constraint Programming for Workforce Scheduling - Interactive | Michael Brenndoerfer | Michael Brenndoerfer\",\"url\":\"https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/cp-sat-rostering-constraint-programming-workforce-scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"What 1,200 Production Deployments Reveal About LLMOps in 2025 - ZenML Blog\",\"url\":\"https://www.zenml.io/blog/what-1200-production-deployments-reveal-about-llmops-in-2025\"}]\n\nI found some relevant results from your search. Here are the key findings:\n\n## CP-SAT Production Case Study\n\nA real-world industrial logistics planning use case within Airbus showcases the storage and management of cargo transported by Beluga aircrafts to and from an aircraft assembly site, with cargo consisting of jigs that must be unloaded/loaded from/to Beluga aircrafts in predefined order and delivered to production lines in predefined order.\n\nThis case addresses planning and decision support by applying a MUS/MCS enumeration algorithm on top of the constraint encoding of planning problems used by the hybrid CP/SAT-based lifted plan-space planner Aries.\n\n## CP-SAT Applications and Implementations\n\nBeyond the Airbus case study, the search results show various CP-SAT implementations in 2024-2025:\n\n- CP-SAT rostering using Google OR-Tools has been applied to solve complex workforce scheduling problems with binary decision variables, coverage constraints, and employee availability for optimal employee shift assignments.\n\n- A sticker printing cost minimization use case employed an OR-Tools CP-SAT optimization approach to minimize printing costs and waste by defining layouts and meeting demands.\n\nThe Airbus logistics planning case study appears to be the most prominent production deployment case specifically highlighted for 2024-2025, featuring in the CP/SAT 2025 workshop materials.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6c31fd31-c9f7-424d-a757-6ea1c270aeda","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:10.440Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"20e3b46c-36de-4752-ad97-7bcb288259f3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
