{"parentUuid":"84036b22-6f73-419b-8545-6197a2012cb3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ku1XjXARDiCv833GVQuZzZ","type":"tool_result","content":"I appreciate your request, but I need to be transparent about what I'm encountering: the content you've provided appears to be a PDF file encoded in binary format, which renders as largely unreadable text when processed as plain text. The raw PDF stream data (with compression, font definitions, and encoded content) doesn't yield the specific information you're asking for about Laurent Perron's slides on CP-SAT.\n\nTo properly extract information about:\n- Industrial use cases\n- Company names using CP-SAT\n- Time budgets\n- Problem scale\n- Parameter tuning recommendations\n\nI would need either:\n1. **A properly decoded PDF or document text** rather than raw PDF binary\n2. **A direct link to the presentation** or document\n3. **The extracted/transcribed text content** from the slides\n\nIf you can provide the readable content or clarify the source material, I'd be happy to extract and summarize those technical details while respecting your constraints on quote length and proper attribution.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 316.3KB) also saved to C:\\Users\\22957\\.claude\\projects\\D--claude-pj-zmd\\7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\\tool-results\\webfetch-1778188221059-qksw1s.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"8fe1efa0-e9a1-4d4c-b87b-0f5a8571eda3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:25.113Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"84036b22-6f73-419b-8545-6197a2012cb3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5c7340a9-eff0-4b79-9558-c726be1f1aa5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014jBZahrTnLTbJeBUoZYwgY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"facility layout problem CP-SAT industrial deployment \"case study\" factory\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"facility layout problem: Topics by Science.gov\",\"url\":\"https://www.science.gov/topicpages/f/facility+layout+problem\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) The facility layout problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/16662725/The_facility_layout_problem\"},{\"title\":\"A comprehensive review of static and dynamic facility layout problems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1367578824000397\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Facility Layout Optimization Using Simulation: A Case Study of a Steel Utensils Industry\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/39965166/Facility_Layout_Optimization_Using_Simulation_A_Case_Study_of_a_Steel_Utensils_Industry\"},{\"title\":\"From theory to application: investigating the generalizability of facility layout problems using a deep reinforcement learning approach | Production Engineering | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11740-025-01352-z\"},{\"title\":\"Layout Design for a Low Capacity Manufacturing Line: A Case Study - Filippo De Carlo, Maria Antonietta Arleo, Orlando Borgia, Mario Tucci, 2013\",\"url\":\"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.5772/56883\"},{\"title\":\"Facility Layout Problem with Alternative Facility Variants\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3417/13/8/5032\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A review of different approaches to the facility layout problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/227297579_A_review_of_different_approaches_to_the_facility_layout_problems\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing Current Facility Layout Case Study\",\"url\":\"https://www.imegllc.com/optimizing-current-facility-layout/\"},{\"title\":\"Facility layout problems: A survey | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/223507648_Facility_layout_problems_A_survey\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query about facility layout problem CP-SAT industrial deployment case studies in factories. Here's a summary of what I found:\n\n## Search Results Overview\n\nThe search returned several relevant academic and technical resources on facility layout problems (FLP) in industrial settings. While the results include general information about facility layout optimization approaches and various case studies, the specific combination of CP-SAT solver with facility layout problems doesn't appear prominently in these particular results.\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**General FLP Information:**\nThe facility layout problem (FLP) is a combinatorial optimization problem that involves finding an optimal arrangement of machines, workstations, and material handling systems within a manufacturing facility.\n\n**Industrial Case Studies:**\nThe search identified several practical case studies:\n- Dalia industries have been selected as a case study to implement integration with the factory divided into two main different areas: the whole facility (layout A), and the manufacturing area (layout B).\n- The utensils industry case study presents a typical work-flow shop based production system, with current and proposed factory layouts simulated using ARENA software.\n- Fashion production lines have been redesigned using systematic layout planning approaches and lean reengineering activities compared against company designs.\n\n**Modern Approaches:**\nReinforcement learning models trained on a limited subset of facility layout problems can generalize to structurally distinct instances, which is promising for scalable deployment in production planning.\n\nIf you're specifically looking for CP-SAT solver applications in facility layout problems, you may need to search more specialized optimization or Google OR-Tools documentation resources, as the general academic literature in this search doesn't prominently feature CP-SAT deployments.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6f553324-7e79-4fc0-b214-d246050852b7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:27.046Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5c7340a9-eff0-4b79-9558-c726be1f1aa5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"38bf1dca-8391-453c-85ae-0f040778d0e5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FZzsHYW7x4nF5evnqVwQXh","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"container loading 2D 3D bin packing OR-Tools CP-SAT logistics company production\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"3D Bin Packing in Logistics: How It Works and Why\",\"url\":\"https://www.optioryx.com/blog/3d-bin-packing\"},{\"title\":\"A three-dimensional container loading algorithm for solving logistics packing problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2192437625000160\"},{\"title\":\"3DPACK.ING | AI-Powered 3D Container & Truck Loading Calculator & Packing Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://3dpack.ing/\"},{\"title\":\"Packing | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/pack\"},{\"title\":\"Truck Packer • 3D Load Planning Built for Real-World Logistics\",\"url\":\"https://www.truckpacker.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Bin Packing Optimization That Works | 3DBinPacking Blog\",\"url\":\"https://www.3dbinpacking.com/en/blog/bin-packing-optimization-strategies/\"},{\"title\":\"Bin packing problem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bin_packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"A Constructive Heuristic Algorithm for 3D Bin Packing of Irregular\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2206.15116\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - dwave-examples/3d-bin-packing: Use the minimum number of bins to pack items with different dimensions, weights and properties. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dwave-examples/3d-bin-packing\"},{\"title\":\"Solving a 3D bin packing problem with stacking constraints - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0360835223008380\"}]\n\nI've completed a web search for your query on container loading, 2D/3D bin packing, OR-Tools CP-SAT, and logistics. Here's a summary of the relevant findings:\n\n## Key Resources Found\n\n**OR-Tools and Optimization Libraries:**\nOR-Tools provides solvers and algorithms for tackling various packing problem types, including knapsack and bin packing. The Google Developers documentation offers guidance on implementing these solutions for packing problems.\n\n**Problem Definition:**\nIn logistics, 3D bin packing is the problem of arranging items into containers so they fit and ship efficiently, either into boxes (cartonization) or onto pallets (palletization). Three-dimensional bin packing underlies \"cartonization,\" where software selects a shipping carton and a feasible packing arrangement for a set of items; closely related industrial problems include container and pallet loading.\n\n**Real-World Applications:**\nLogistics companies use it to cut packaging and transport costs by fitting items into boxes, building denser pallets, and planning fuller loads for trucks, containers, and aircrafts, while respecting size, weight limits, orientation rules, carrier rate structures and many other constraints.\n\n**Software Solutions:**\nThe search revealed several specialized platforms like 3DBinPacking.com, Truck Packer, and 3DPACK.ING that implement bin packing optimization. 3DBinPacking is tailored specifically to 2D and 3D bin packing challenges, supporting real-time API integration and large-scale data processing, and is particularly well-suited for logistics, e-commerce, and manufacturing environments where speed and usability are essential.\n\n**Algorithm Approaches:**\nTruck Packer uses 3D bin-packing and placement heuristics tuned for real trailers, bays, and touring loads.\n\nThe search results show active research and development in this area, with both academic papers and production-ready commercial solutions available.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3393d134-dbb5-4767-82f2-e0d135157ecd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:28.752Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"38bf1dca-8391-453c-85ae-0f040778d0e5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
