{"parentUuid":"3071fa2e-2af5-46cb-b233-e81389efdf10","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013jb7FK2wUT1CSmnfrCtegd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Po3absafaMCJ35iBpvSgmf","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CP-SAT vs Gurobi CPLEX industrial benchmark \"real world\" production"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4290,"cache_read_input_tokens":26403,"output_tokens":321,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4290},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":321,"cache_read_input_tokens":26403,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4290,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4290,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caotrv2P4yiYjGea7tZU6","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"244dccd0-262f-4389-a7be-4ea34ecb2c4b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:33.320Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d1ab72f1-523a-4ca1-80ac-4543e6aa7581","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C8vrK1dDTE8wneeodCuL8P","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"OR-Tools\" \"CP-SAT\" production deployment company experience nurse scheduling shift\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Employee Scheduling | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/scheduling/employee_scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"Solving the Nurse Rostering Problem using Google OR-Tools | by Mahdi Mobini | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@mobini/solving-the-nurse-rostering-problem-using-google-or-tools-755689b877c0\"},{\"title\":\"Solver Max - Nurse rostering in OR-tools CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://www.solvermax.com/resources/models/staff-scheduling/nurse-rostering-in-or-tools-cp-sat-solver\"},{\"title\":\"Application of Constraint Programming with Satisfiability in Nurse Scheduling\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2673-4591/134/1/32\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Rostering: Complete Guide to Constraint Programming for Workforce Scheduling - Interactive | Michael Brenndoerfer | Michael Brenndoerfer\",\"url\":\"https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/cp-sat-rostering-constraint-programming-workforce-scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"Python employee scheduling does not give any solutions if num_nurses != num_shifts · Issue #932 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/932\"},{\"title\":\"Nurse rostering with competences · Issue #991 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/991\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Programming with Google OR-Tools\",\"url\":\"http://didattica.cs.unicam.it/lib/exe/fetch.php?media=didattica:ay2122:lcp:or_tools_03_practiceexercise_and_assignment.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Nurse scheduling CpSolver stuck in some solutions · Issue #1300 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1300\"},{\"title\":\"Shift Optimization with Google OR Tools | by Işıl Berfin Koparan | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@isilberfin/shift-optimization-with-google-or-tools-f23da014e480\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about OR-Tools, CP-SAT, and nurse scheduling deployment:\n\n## OR-Tools and CP-SAT for Nurse Scheduling\n\nThe CP-SAT solver can be used to solve employee scheduling problems, and the models are solved using the CP-SAT solver for nurse rostering problems.\n\n### Production Deployment and Company Experience\n\nFor production systems, Google OR-Tools provides a robust CP-SAT solver that can handle complex rostering problems with advanced features, allowing implementation of a complete rostering system that demonstrates real-world capabilities.\n\n### Practical Nurse Scheduling Applications\n\nSolving the Nurse Rostering Problem is one of the most critical steps of workforce planning in healthcare systems such as hospitals, clinics, and long-term care facilities. The Google OR-Tools Constraint Programming with Satisfiability (CP-SAT) solver has been applied to the nurse scheduling problem to efficiently generate feasible and high-quality schedules under complex real-world constraints.\n\n### Key Advantages\n\nNurse scheduling must simultaneously satisfy multiple complex constraints—hard constraints that must never be violated and soft constraints that should be satisfied as much as possible—and CP-SAT can handle both types of constraints properly.\n\nThe search results show multiple academic papers and production examples demonstrating how CP-SAT is being used to solve real-world nurse scheduling problems with various constraints and requirements.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2714db9b-0a15-491c-b994-a71bcc6b9a71","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:37.681Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d1ab72f1-523a-4ca1-80ac-4543e6aa7581","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3071fa2e-2af5-46cb-b233-e81389efdf10","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ur5s1KZXqoKdFpRaGuso8c","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"we use CP-SAT\" engineering blog reddit hackernews production OR-Tools\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"I’m a bit uncertain about what Google OR-Tools is…it *seems* to be some sort of ... | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=22582688\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/README.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/docs/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Rostering: Complete Guide to Constraint Programming for Workforce Scheduling - Interactive | Michael Brenndoerfer | Michael Brenndoerfer\",\"url\":\"https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/cp-sat-rostering-constraint-programming-workforce-scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"A practical introduction to Constraint Programming using CP-SAT and Python\",\"url\":\"https://pganalyze.com/blog/a-practical-introduction-to-constraint-programming-using-cp-sat\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Multi_Threading crash · Issue #2131 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/2131\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solver vs. CP solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Pa5eQUoLnow\"},{\"title\":\"Ask HN: What are some great engineering blogs? | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=29237308\"}]\n\nI found several relevant search results about CP-SAT and OR-Tools. Here are the key findings:\n\n## CP-SAT Solver Capabilities\n\nThe CP-SAT solver has consistently won the Minizinc challenge the last few years and the routing library is a great local search framework.\n\n## Production Use Cases\n\nCP-SAT is used inside pganalyze Indexing Engine and pganalyze Index Advisor, with pganalyze sharing this knowledge to help the wider programming community utilize solvers like CP-SAT in practice.\n\nFor workforce scheduling, the solve time remains reasonable even for complex problems, typically completing within 30 seconds, which is suitable for production use.\n\n## Educational Resources\n\nCP-SAT is recently being used as the first optimization solver due to its high-level interface, which is much easier for beginners to grasp. There's also a CP-SAT Primer resource available for using and understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver.\n\nThe search results show CP-SAT is being used in real production systems for optimization problems, supported by educational resources and comprehensive documentation across multiple programming languages.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b0400684-3509-4c0e-a415-359b1c51b70b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:39.594Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3071fa2e-2af5-46cb-b233-e81389efdf10","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b9c95934-01fa-41ee-afeb-4c596c302060","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U3f2FEb2jA7CQ198GnpvTX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT semiconductor fab scheduling industrial JSSP FJSSP case study\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Fab-Wide Scheduling of Semiconductor Plants: A Large-Scale Industrial Deployment Case Study | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10015364\"},{\"title\":\"Scalability of Reinforcement Learning Methods for ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.11135\"},{\"title\":\"Fab-Wide Scheduling of Semiconductor Plants: A Large-Scale Industrial Deployment Case Study | Blog & News | Flexciton\",\"url\":\"https://flexciton.com/blog-news/fab-wide-scheduling-of-semiconductor-plants-case-study\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A simulation optimization framework to solve Stochastic Flexible Job-Shop Scheduling Problems—Case: Semiconductor manufacturing\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/376254626_A_simulation_optimization_framework_to_solve_Stochastic_Flexible_Job-Shop_Scheduling_Problems-Case_Semiconductor_manufacturing\"},{\"title\":\"Types of Flexible Job Shop Scheduling: A Constraint Programming Experiment\",\"url\":\"https://www.scitepress.org/Papers/2022/108499/108499.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GAILS: an effective multi-object job shop scheduler based on genetic algorithm and iterative local search | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-51778-1\"},{\"title\":\"A simulation optimization framework to solve Stochastic Flexible Job-Shop Scheduling Problems—Case: : Semiconductor manufacturing: Computers and Operations Research: Vol 163, No C\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1016/j.cor.2023.106508\"},{\"title\":\"Comparison of scheduling problems SMSP PMSP FSSP FFSSP JSSP FJSSP CJSSP | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Comparison-of-scheduling-problems-SMSP-PMSP-FSSP-FFSSP-JSSP-FJSSP-CJSSP_tbl1_394027801\"},{\"title\":\"A simulation optimization framework to solve Stochastic Flexible Job-Shop Scheduling Problems—Case: Semiconductor manufacturing - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0305054823003726\"},{\"title\":\"A Greedy Search Based Ant Colony Optimization Algorithm for\",\"url\":\"https://www.scitepress.org/Papers/2024/128131/128131.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found regarding CP-SAT semiconductor fab scheduling with JSSP and FJSSP case studies:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### Industrial Fab-Wide Scheduling Case Study\n\nA novel fab-wide scheduling approach has been developed for large semiconductor manufacturing plants, addressing the challenge of scheduling thousands of wafers on hundreds of machines across several steps while respecting operational constraints such as photolithography reticles, timelinks and flow control limits. Illustrative examples and aggregate statistics were obtained during trials at Seagate Springtown. This approach can result in substantial cycle time improvements compared to myopic dispatch methods and marked reduction in manual intervention for controlling flows.\n\n### Semiconductor Fab Scheduling Problem Types\n\nResearch has addressed Stochastic Flexible Job-Shop Scheduling Problems (SFJSSP) in the context of semiconductor manufacturing. Within the front-end fab of the semiconductor industry, the photolithography workstation is the well-known bottleneck process.\n\n### Photolithography as FJSSP\n\nFJSSP is an extension of JSSP where operations can be conducted on a set of compatible machines, and FJSSP is therefore at least as complex as JSSP. The photolithography workstation has three specific constraints: machines are competent for different recipes (machine process capability constraints), certain machines are required for quality purposes (machine dedication constraints), and the number of times a reticle is shared between different layer productions should be limited (maximum reticles sharing constraints).\n\n### Large-Scale Semiconductor Applications\n\nResearch has evaluated scheduling approaches using classical FJSSP benchmarks as well as large-scale instances with about 10,000 operations from the domain of semiconductor production scheduling.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"265bc62f-91ff-4058-871f-12a0d704060f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:40.173Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b9c95934-01fa-41ee-afeb-4c596c302060","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"244dccd0-262f-4389-a7be-4ea34ecb2c4b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Po3absafaMCJ35iBpvSgmf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT vs Gurobi CPLEX industrial benchmark \"real world\" production\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Hexaly, CP Optimizer, OR-Tools, Gurobi, Cplex on very large-scale instances of the Job Shop Scheduling Problem (JSSP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks/hexaly-vs-cp-optimizer-vs-or-tools-on-the-job-shop-scheduling-problem-jssp\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding Fundamental Differences Between MIP and CP Solvers in or-tools Context\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/NoGdc_MiXT0\"},{\"title\":\"Comparison of Cplex 11.0, Cplex 10.2, CBC 2.2, and SCIP 1.1 with... | Download Table\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Comparison-of-Cplex-110-Cplex-102-CBC-22-and-SCIP-11-with-different-LP-solvers_tbl4_225664381\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CBC: A Practical Guide to the COIN-OR Solver | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cbc-a-practical-guide-to-the-coin-or-solver-fe5c1408d802\"},{\"title\":\"Ask HN: Do you use an optimization solver? Which one? Do you like it? | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=31099186\"},{\"title\":\"What is the difference between Cplex and Gurobi? | ResearchGate\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/post/What_is_the_difference_between_Cplex_and_Gurobi\"},{\"title\":\"Wageningen University - Department of Social Sciences\",\"url\":\"https://edepot.wur.nl/638173\"},{\"title\":\"Automatic constraint programming solver selection method based on machine learning for the cable tree wiring problem - Zhang - 2024 - The Journal of Engineering - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://ietresearch.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1049/tje2.12368\"},{\"title\":\"Gurobi\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/pdfs/benchmarks.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CP-SAT vs Gurobi and CPLEX in industrial benchmark comparisons:\n\n## General Performance Characteristics\n\nOn the MiniZinc benchmark, Gurobi is considered slightly better on pure linear problems, while CP-SAT is better on all constraint programming problems. CP-SAT is currently the best CP solver and a very good ILP solver, though it does not support continuous variables (unless they are implied integers), in which case Gurobi should be used.\n\n## Job Shop Scheduling Benchmark\n\nA notable industrial benchmark comes from a comparison on the Job Shop Scheduling Problem (JSSP):\n\nA benchmark compared Hexaly 14.0 with IBM ILOG CP Optimizer 12.10.0, Google OR-Tools CP-SAT 9.14, Gurobi 11.0.1, and IBM ILOG CPLEX 22.1.0. In this test, OR-Tools, Gurobi, and CPLEX failed to deliver feasible solutions within 6 hours of running time on very large-scale instances with 1,000 jobs and 1,000 machines.\n\n## Cable Tree Wiring Problem\n\nIn a more recent industrial application study, CPLEX was the only solver that could find solutions for all satisfiable instances tested, while OR-Tools yielded the highest number of optimal solutions and achieved faster solving speeds.\n\n## Commercial vs. Open-Source Trade-offs\n\nGurobi and CPLEX are significantly faster, especially on large problems, but they cost thousands of dollars per year and have nicer APIs and better documentation.\n\nThe choice between these solvers depends heavily on the specific problem type—constraint programming problems favor CP-SAT, while pure linear programming problems may favor the commercial solvers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ab9fafc7-d540-40e6-9960-c601d66a8173","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:42.766Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"244dccd0-262f-4389-a7be-4ea34ecb2c4b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
