{"parentUuid":"44d1178b-c472-44f5-a1cd-88eebec00ad0","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_012MmHKHcgT5DLYiUZyKZJH3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FtrzXyWEWc4N5FYsRAQXcx","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"OR-Tools\" \"CP-SAT\" Airbus aerospace warehouse production talk slides"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6111,"cache_read_input_tokens":30693,"output_tokens":477,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6111},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":477,"cache_read_input_tokens":30693,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6111,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6111,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caotswv25vW7HmAPVbDS1","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"8f696850-4d62-4ddd-bc24-a841d7fbb83e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:49.877Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"52bde363-8a85-4a97-95c6-dbb77e23558c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UMXKo95p6AVT5H9DFQCv2G","type":"tool_result","content":"# Fab-Wide Scheduling Deployment Analysis\n\n## Solver & Technical Details\nThe article does not specify the optimization solver used (e.g., CP-SAT, CPLEX, or other). Technical implementation details remain undisclosed in this case study.\n\n## Problem Scale\nThe deployment involved \"Seagate's Springtown fab,\" which produces approximately 25% of global recording head demand. Specific metrics on job counts or machine quantities are not provided.\n\n## Time Budget & Parameters\nNo information about computational time budgets or specific parameter configurations is disclosed in the article.\n\n## Deployment Information\n**Company/Fab:** Seagate Technology, Springtown facility (Northern Ireland)\n\n**Timeline:** \n- Trial period: March–May 2022\n- Full operational deployment: June 2022 onwards (24/7 continuous operation)\n\n## Performance Metrics\n\nThe study measured impact through three approaches:\n\n1. **Ad hoc rule reduction:** \"The number of ad hoc rule transactions averaged less than 150 per week\" post-deployment, representing \"a decrease of over 300%\" compared to pre-deployment baseline\n\n2. **Additional improvements noted:** The article indicates \"substantial improvements in throughput and cycle times\" were achieved, though detailed numerical results are reserved for future publications\n\n3. **Methodology:** Rather than traditional A/B testing, researchers examined \"deep dives on specific toolsets,\" simulation comparisons, and manual intervention volume changes due to \"dynamic fab conditions\""}]},"uuid":"d8f54130-f5de-400a-b9b8-97516c9eea54","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:53.918Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"52bde363-8a85-4a97-95c6-dbb77e23558c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"57116bb1-dfa7-49e7-bb78-c5e50ceeaf36","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PZqraZyUu7KpB8x62JgCqk","type":"tool_result","content":"# pganalyze's Use of CP-SAT\n\nBased on the article provided, here's what I found regarding pganalyze's implementation:\n\n## Production Application\n\npganalyze uses CP-SAT in their **Indexing Engine** and **Index Advisor** products. As stated in the article: \"This is the first part in a two part series on constraint programming, used inside pganalyze Indexing Engine and pganalyze Index Advisor.\"\n\n## Problem Being Solved\n\nThe second article in this series (referenced but not included in the content) addresses \"Constraint Programming in Action: Optimizing Postgres Index Selection,\" indicating they use CP-SAT to optimize database index selection decisions.\n\n## Information Not Available\n\nThe article does not provide specific details about:\n- **Time budget** for solving\n- **Problem scale** (number of indexes, tables, or constraints)\n- **Parameter tuning** specifics\n\n## Context\n\nThe article frames CP-SAT as a declarative approach to \"discrete optimization problems\" and demonstrates its capability through a practical employee scheduling example, positioning constraint programming as suitable for real-world optimization challenges like warehouse location selection and route optimization."}]},"uuid":"db8efd90-ff54-4332-beb0-d31e7a962ca5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:54.575Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"57116bb1-dfa7-49e7-bb78-c5e50ceeaf36","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"44d1178b-c472-44f5-a1cd-88eebec00ad0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BqQR5fPhtjQ4fMgzUVdjxt","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT num_search_workers linearization_level production tuning best practices\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.ortools — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/cp_optimizer/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Rostering: Complete Guide to Constraint Programming for Workforce Scheduling - Interactive | Michael Brenndoerfer | Michael Brenndoerfer\",\"url\":\"https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/cp-sat-rostering-constraint-programming-workforce-scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. · Issue #3662 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662\"},{\"title\":\"Expected time to evaluate model (feasibility)\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/acul1GgXqf8\"},{\"title\":\"A practical introduction to Constraint Programming using CP-SAT and Python\",\"url\":\"https://pganalyze.com/blog/a-practical-introduction-to-constraint-programming-using-cp-sat\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT claims to find optimal solution to a MILP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4fcAuWiIUFA\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CP-SAT `num_search_workers`, `linearization_level`, and production tuning best practices:\n\n## Key Parameters\n\n**num_search_workers**: You can control the parallelization of CP-SAT by setting the number of search workers. By default, CP-SAT leverages all available cores (including hyperthreading).\n\n**linearization_level**: The portfolio includes solvers with different linearization levels, such as default_lp (linearization_level:1), no_lp (linearization_level:0), and max_lp (linearization_level:2).\n\n## Portfolio Solver Architecture\n\nCP-SAT uses a portfolio of different subsolvers, each configured with varying settings (e.g., different levels of linearization) to solve the model. There is some information exchange between the different workers, but it does not split the solution space into different parts, thus, it does not parallelize the branch-and-bound algorithm as MIP-solvers do.\n\n## Production Tuning Best Practices\n\nIt is important not to modify the parameters at the top level, as this would affect all subsolvers. Doing so could disrupt the balance of the portfolio, potentially activating costly techniques for the LNS-workers, which could slow them down. Additionally, you risk creating a default subsolver incompatible with your model, causing CP-SAT to exclude most or all subsolvers.\n\nDecreasing the number of search workers can actually improve the runtime for some problems, which indicates that selecting the right subsolvers that are best fitted for your problem can be worth a shot.\n\nFor production systems: Implement timeout mechanisms and fallback strategies for cases where the solver cannot find a solution within acceptable time limits. Consider using parallel processing for multiple problem instances or implementing incremental solving where small changes to schedules are optimized rather than complete re-optimization.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"86de982a-0a23-4d2c-a852-8b0f6574ab63","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:57.346Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"44d1178b-c472-44f5-a1cd-88eebec00ad0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8f696850-4d62-4ddd-bc24-a841d7fbb83e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FtrzXyWEWc4N5FYsRAQXcx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"OR-Tools\" \"CP-SAT\" Airbus aerospace warehouse production talk slides\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Satair - A global supplier of aircraft parts, services & solutions | Satair\",\"url\":\"https://www.satair.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Satair opens the largest warehouse facility in Airbus Group | Airbus\",\"url\":\"https://www.aircraft.airbus.com/en/newsroom/press-releases/2024-09-satair-opens-the-largest-warehouse-facility-in-airbus-group\"},{\"title\":\"Aerospace Supply Chain Management | ARTS Group\",\"url\":\"https://arts.aero/aerospace-supply-chain-management\"},{\"title\":\"Developing Smart Tools for the Airbus Factory of the Future - NI\",\"url\":\"https://www.ni.com/en/solutions/aerospace-defense/case-studies/developing-smart-tools-for-the-airbus-factory-of-the-future.html\"},{\"title\":\"Airbus Approved Suppliers List 2018 | PDF | Airbus | Aerospace\",\"url\":\"https://www.scribd.com/document/419739484/Airbus-Approved-Suppliers-List\"},{\"title\":\"Airbus Space Equipment | Space | Airbus\",\"url\":\"https://www.airbus.com/en/products-services/space/space-equipment\"},{\"title\":\"Specialized Tools for Boeing and Airbus Aircraft | Pacific Tool\",\"url\":\"https://pacifictool.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Airbus - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Airbus\"},{\"title\":\"Aerospace Logistics: Building for Growth - Inbound Logistics\",\"url\":\"https://www.inboundlogistics.com/articles/aerospace-logistics-building-for-growth/\"},{\"title\":\"Smart aerospace industry solutions - Atlas Copco USA\",\"url\":\"https://www.atlascopco.com/en-us/itba/industry-solutions/aerospace-industry\"}]\n\nThe search results I found don't contain specific information about OR-Tools, CP-SAT, Airbus warehouse production talk slides. Let me try a more targeted search focusing specifically on OR-Tools and CP-SAT.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Google AI’s OR-Tools CP-SAT Solver unofficial tutorial Bobak Pezeshki\",\"url\":\"https://ics.uci.edu/~dechter/courses/ics-275/fall-2020/slides/OR-Tools_CP-SAT_Solver_Tutorial.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Optimization | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solver vs. CP solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Pa5eQUoLnow\"}]\n\nBased on my web searches, I found general information about OR-Tools and CP-SAT, but I was unable to locate specific presentation slides about an Airbus aerospace warehouse production talk using OR-Tools and CP-SAT.\n\nThe search results show that:\n\n- OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver handles integer programming problems, and CP-SAT overcomes many weaknesses of classical solvers and provides a viable alternative to MIP-solvers\n\n- Scheduling problems are well-suited for the CP-SAT solver, which could apply to warehouse and production scenarios\n\n- There is a documented tutorial on OR-Tools CP-SAT, but it doesn't specifically address Airbus applications\n\nHowever, I could not find the specific presentation slides you're looking for that discuss Airbus warehouse production optimization using OR-Tools and CP-SAT. It's possible that:\n\n1. This may be a proprietary or internal Airbus presentation not publicly available\n2. The presentation may be on a specialized conference or technical workshop site\n3. The materials may use different terminology in their titles\n\nIf you have additional details about where this presentation was delivered (e.g., a conference name, venue, or date), I could perform a more targeted search.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9c49574b-d432-4576-865a-d07e48aa9161","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:57.757Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8f696850-4d62-4ddd-bc24-a841d7fbb83e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
