{"parentUuid":"f761a763-34dd-4c4f-9921-168910698525","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0f373ebb-a92e-4bba-8942-d03ed7b7aa78","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RzyS9y8BjC8pvJ1JPc1iJo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"CP-SAT\" OR \"or-tools\" rostering nurse hospital deployment \"30 seconds\" OR \"1 hour\" OR \"overnight\"\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Solver Max - Nurse rostering in OR-tools CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://www.solvermax.com/resources/models/staff-scheduling/nurse-rostering-in-or-tools-cp-sat-solver\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Rostering: Complete Guide to Constraint Programming for Workforce Scheduling - Interactive | Michael Brenndoerfer | Michael Brenndoerfer\",\"url\":\"https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/cp-sat-rostering-constraint-programming-workforce-scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"Nurse rostering with competences · Issue #991 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/991\"},{\"title\":\"Solving the Nurse Rostering Problem using Google OR-Tools | by Mahdi Mobini | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@mobini/solving-the-nurse-rostering-problem-using-google-or-tools-755689b877c0\"},{\"title\":\"SOLVING NURSE SCHEDULING PROBLEM USING CONSTRAINT PROGRAMMING TECHNIQUE\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1902.01193\"},{\"title\":\"Employee Scheduling | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/scheduling/employee_scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"Artificial intelligence and end user tools to develop a nurse duty roster scheduling system - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9305000/\"},{\"title\":\"Artificial intelligence and end user tools to develop a nurse duty roster scheduling system - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S235201322200045X\"},{\"title\":\"Using OR-Tools When Solving the Nurse Scheduling Problem | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-53025-8_30\"},{\"title\":\"A Brief Study of the Nurse Scheduling Problem (NSP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.math.cmu.edu/~af1p/Teaching/OR2/Projects/P23/ORProject_Final_Copy.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the findings related to CP-SAT, OR-Tools, and nurse rostering with relevant deployment timeframes:\n\n## Deployment Time Performance\n\nThe CP-SAT solver typically completes nurse rostering solutions within 30 seconds for problems with 5 employees, 4 shift types, and 5 days (100 total decision variables), which is suitable for production use.\n\nFor problems with fewer than 100 variables, 10-30 seconds is usually sufficient.\n\nA hospital-based system generated schedules within 1 minute under both hard and soft constraint optimization.\n\n## Key Applications\n\nIn healthcare settings, CP-SAT excels at handling complex nurse scheduling requirements including mandatory rest periods, skill level matching, and labor law compliance.\n\nCP-SAT is generally efficient for many rostering problems, often finding good solutions quickly even for large-scale problems with hundreds of employees and thousands of time slots.\n\n## Production Implementation\n\nGoogle OR-Tools is an economical and open-source operational research tool suitable for operation research optimization and can be employed to tackle constraint programming problems such as scheduling.\n\nThe search results show multiple real-world hospital implementations using CP-SAT and OR-Tools for nurse rostering, with deployment times ranging from under 30 seconds for smaller problems to 1 minute for full hospital-scale scheduling systems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ce7fcfea-ef5d-475f-a6be-0d8418a74a32","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:07.447Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f761a763-34dd-4c4f-9921-168910698525","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"250d2fd0-2c1f-42dd-a468-dc18b2afa35f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0f373ebb-a92e-4bba-8942-d03ed7b7aa78","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BNoF8R88DH8okB6cMDecLu","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"CPAIOR\" OR \"CP conference\" industrial talk OR-Tools real deployment manufacturing 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2024\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2024\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2024 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2024/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2024 | Artificial Intelligence Institute for Advances in Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.ai4opt.org/news-events/cpaior-2024\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR Conference Series\",\"url\":\"https://cpaior.org/\"},{\"title\":\"2024 - CPAIOR Conference\",\"url\":\"https://cpaior.org/2024\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2024 - About\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2024/about\"},{\"title\":\"Call for Participation: CPAIOR 2024\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/icaps-conference/c/Bl_4ZwW8eRo\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR: Integration of AI and OR Techniques in Constraint Programming 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=574\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2024 : International Conference on the Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/servlet/event.showcfp?copyownerid=90704&eventid=175986\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2024 - Master Class\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2024/master-class_1\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CPAIOR 2024, which was the 21st International Conference on the Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research held May 28-31, 2024, in Uppsala, Sweden.\n\nThe aim of CPAIOR is to bring together researchers from Constraint Programming (CP), Artificial Intelligence (AI), and Operations Research (OR) to present new techniques, applications, and theoretical & practical insights from a wide array of problems. The conference strongly encourages regular papers or experience reports showcasing CP/AI/OR techniques on challenging real-world applications.\n\nThe conference program included several highlights: a Master Class on Quantum Computing for CP, AI, and OR, keynote talks by Elina Rönnberg, Tias Guns, and Giacomo Nannicini, presentations of 42 accepted peer-reviewed papers, and two poster sessions for extended abstracts.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific information about industrial talks related to OR-Tools, real deployment scenarios in manufacturing, or other specific manufacturing case studies from CPAIOR 2024. If you're looking for details about specific industrial talks or OR-Tools presentations at the conference, you may want to check the official conference proceedings or website directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4e3921b2-ed8d-4abe-9e6d-e5d70d25d22e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:08.269Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"250d2fd0-2c1f-42dd-a468-dc18b2afa35f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c2e3917d-b471-435e-a9a4-8d9bd518ee27","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0f373ebb-a92e-4bba-8942-d03ed7b7aa78","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017k8frEzDRJDCrB1zfwmKPx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Hacker News \"CP-SAT\" production used optimization solver discussion\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"I’m a bit uncertain about what Google OR-Tools is…it *seems* to be some sort of ... | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=22582688\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Yes, OR-tools has a lot of solvers. The solver I talked about is the CP-SAT solv... | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=32807583\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"A practical introduction to constraint programming using CP-SAT and Python | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40867746\"},{\"title\":\"Modern SAT solvers: fast, neat and underused (2018) | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=36087464\"},{\"title\":\"Modern SAT solvers: fast, neat and underused | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=19953213\"},{\"title\":\"📈 #76 Optimizing with Google OR-Tools: strategies and insights from three years of real-world experience\",\"url\":\"https://www.feasible.club/p/76-optimizing-with-google-or-tools\"}]\n\nI found several relevant results about CP-SAT and its use. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## About CP-SAT\n\nThe CP-SAT solver has consistently won the Minizinc challenge the last few years, indicating its strong performance in optimization challenges.\n\n## Architecture and Capabilities\n\nThe CP-SAT solver is architectured around five components: The base layer is a clause learning SAT solver. Above the SAT layer sits a Constraint Programming (CP) module with Boolean, integer and interval variables, and standard integer, scheduling and routing constraints. Alongside the CP solver, a simplex provides a global linear relaxation.\n\n## Production Usage\n\nThere's evidence of real-world production adoption. One user described learning about managing interval variables and the CP-SAT solver's parameterization, then starting to use it for testing ideas that became proof of concepts which evolved into production mode, with three years of usage. \n\nThe solver is particularly useful for optimization problems in planning, operational applications, or logistics that have lots of boolean decision variables, integer variables with small domains, and logic constraints that relate them with nonlinear functions.\n\nThe search results include several Hacker News discussions about CP-SAT and optimization solvers, though not a single dedicated thread specifically matching your exact query.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"881b83b2-4c8f-4fce-8a4f-1cf7f9a92399","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:09.535Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c2e3917d-b471-435e-a9a4-8d9bd518ee27","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c6f9c140-bbda-4e43-b15f-69a1e8c744af","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0f373ebb-a92e-4bba-8942-d03ed7b7aa78","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VFuYVeAqkhThV9hLrNANq6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Google ads bidding CP-SAT or-tools data center placement scheduling production\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"About bid adjustments - Google Ads Help\",\"url\":\"https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/2732132?hl=en\"},{\"title\":\"Bidding - Google Ads Help\",\"url\":\"https://support.google.com/google-ads/faq/10286469?hl=en\"},{\"title\":\"About adjusting your keyword bids - Google Ads Help\",\"url\":\"https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/2472712?hl=en-GB\"},{\"title\":\"Key Considerations for Google Ads Automated Bidding - Karooya\",\"url\":\"https://www.karooya.com/blog/best-practices-for-google-ads-automated-bidding/\"},{\"title\":\"Smart Moves: A Guide to Google Ads Bidding Strategies - Linear\",\"url\":\"https://lineardesign.com/blog/bidding-strategy-google-ads/\"},{\"title\":\"Google Ads Bid Management 101: A Beginner’s Guide to Higher Conversions\",\"url\":\"https://www.optmyzr.com/blog/google-ads-bid-management/\"},{\"title\":\"The Right Bid Adjustments for Your Google Ads Bid Strategy\",\"url\":\"https://www.optmyzr.com/blog/which-bid-adjustments-work-with-my-bid-strategy-on-google-ads/\"},{\"title\":\"Set up Smart Bidding - Google Ads Help\",\"url\":\"https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/10893605?hl=en\"},{\"title\":\"Google Ads Bid Strategy: Manual or Automated?\",\"url\":\"https://savvyrevenue.com/blog/automated-bid-management-google-ads/\"},{\"title\":\"Navigating Smart Bidding in Google Ads : Your FAQ Handbook - Karooya\",\"url\":\"https://www.karooya.com/blog/smart-bidding-google-ads-faqs/\"}]\n\nThe search results I found focus primarily on Google Ads bidding strategies and bid adjustments, but they don't contain information about CP-SAT, OR-Tools, data center placement scheduling, or production optimization—which are technical constraint programming and optimization topics. \n\nLet me search with different terms that focus on the technical optimization aspects:\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Optimization | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Solving a CP Problem | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_example\"},{\"title\":\"Google AI’s OR-Tools CP-SAT Solver unofficial tutorial Bobak Pezeshki\",\"url\":\"https://ics.uci.edu/~dechter/courses/ics-275/fall-2020/slides/OR-Tools_CP-SAT_Solver_Tutorial.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/or-tools: Google's Operations Research tools: · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OR-Tools\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Constraint Programming Solver | google/or-tools | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/google/or-tools/4.1-cp-sat-constraint-programming-solver\"}]\n\nNow let me search for information specifically about data center placement and scheduling optimization:\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Full article: An effective scheduling in data centres for efficient CPU usage and service level agreement fulfilment using machine learning\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/09540091.2021.1926929\"},{\"title\":\"Full article: Virtual Machine Placement Using JAYA Optimization Algorithm\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/08839514.2019.1689714\"},{\"title\":\"Hyperscale Data Center Construction Scheduling | Optimize Timelines | StruxHubStruxHub\",\"url\":\"https://struxhub.com/blog/hyperscale-data-centers-optimizing-multi-tier-construction-scheduling-for-seamless-project-execution/\"},{\"title\":\"Data Center Optimization: Strategies for Improving Efficiency and Performance - SwiftTech Solutions\",\"url\":\"https://swifttechsolutions.com/swifttech-blog/managed-it-services/data-center-optimization-strategies-for-improving-efficiency-and-performance/\"},{\"title\":\"Reinforcement learning for data center energy efficiency optimization: A systematic literature review and research roadmap - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306261925004647\"},{\"title\":\"How to Optimize Data Centers for the Automated World\",\"url\":\"https://www1.raritan.com/DASHBOARD-How-to-Optimize-Data-Centers-for-the-Automated-World.html\"},{\"title\":\"AI-driven job scheduling in cloud computing: a comprehensive review | Artificial Intelligence Review | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10462-025-11208-8\"},{\"title\":\"A Deep Reinforcement Learning Approach to the Optimization of Data Center Task Scheduling - Che - 2020 - Complexity - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1155/2020/3046769\"},{\"title\":\"Data center optimization: Is it time for a refresh?\",\"url\":\"https://www.ibm.com/think/insights/data-center-optimization\"},{\"title\":\"Scaling bigger, faster, cheaper data centers with smarter designs\",\"url\":\"https://www.mckinsey.com/industries/private-capital/our-insights/scaling-bigger-faster-cheaper-data-centers-with-smarter-designs\"}]\n\nBased on my web search results, I found comprehensive information about CP-SAT, OR-Tools, and data center optimization topics. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## CP-SAT Solver and OR-Tools\n\nThe CP-SAT solver is designed for integer programming problems and is generally faster than MPSolver. CP-SAT solver is a constraint programming solver that uses SAT (satisfiability) methods.\n\nGoogle Optimization Tools (a.k.a., OR-Tools) is an open-source, fast and portable software suite for solving combinatorial optimization problems. The suite contains: Two constraint programming solver (CP* and CP-SAT); Two linear programming solvers (Glop and PDLP); Wrappers around commercial and other open source solvers, including mixed integer solvers; Bin packing and knapsack algorithms; Algorithms for the Traveling Salesman Problem and Vehicle Routing Problem; Graph algorithms (shortest paths, min cost flow, max flow, linear sum assignment).\n\nThe relatively new CP-SAT of Google's OR-Tools suite shows to overcome many of the weaknesses and provides a viable alternative to MIP-solvers, being competitive for many problems and sometimes even superior. The CP-SAT solver bundled with OR-Tools has been consistently winning gold medals in the MiniZinc Challenge, an international constraint programming competition.\n\n## Data Center Scheduling and Placement\n\nDetermining the optimal placement (allocation) of VMs is an essential aspect of the data center to boost the physical resource utilization to reduce the energy usage while satisfying the service level agreement (SLA).\n\nResearch explores the application of RL/DRL algorithms for optimizing data center energy efficiency, with a focus on optimizing the operation of cooling systems and Information and Communication Technology (ICT) processes, including task scheduling, resource allocation, virtual machine (VM) consolidation/placement, and network traffic control.\n\nAs data center projects get bigger, a generative scheduling tool can be added to the end-to-end delivery model. The tool uses a 4D model of a single data center project to run thousands of iterations of the project schedule and resource plan. It then identifies the optimal sequencing and project resourcing, such as workforce and construction equipment, that can be scaled across a portfolio of data center projects through common construction recipes.\n\nHowever, my search results do not contain any specific information connecting Google Ads bidding to CP-SAT or OR-Tools for data center placement scheduling. The first search about Google Ads bidding returned results about ad bidding strategies, which are separate from the constraint programming and data center optimization topics found in subsequent searches.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ecfd7f01-6f56-4da2-966b-090368f5c35a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:22.844Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c6f9c140-bbda-4e43-b15f-69a1e8c744af","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
