{"parentUuid":"46e6c4d1-a867-466c-8a39-3de02fc550d1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0da025bf-5462-4d88-9ddf-73d39057a5ff","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HRTpVJLtPDxNAZZ99nvXBx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Google OR-Tools \"we use\" OR \"powered by\" production optimization customer testimonial\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"14 Best GEO Agencies To Rank In AI Search - Perceptric\",\"url\":\"https://perceptric.com/blog/best-generative-engine-optimization-agencies/\"},{\"title\":\"Top 7 Generative Engine Optimization Service Providers Ranked (Q2 2026 Update) - GenOptima\",\"url\":\"https://www.gen-optima.com/geo/top-7-generative-engine-optimization-service-providers-ranked/\"},{\"title\":\"Top AI Optimization Agencies | 20North Marketing | 20North\",\"url\":\"https://www.20northmarketing.com/blog/top-ai-optimization-agencies\"},{\"title\":\"10 Best Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) Agencies 2026\",\"url\":\"https://minuttia.com/best-geo-agencies/\"},{\"title\":\"Google Optimize is Back? It’s 2025 & Google Is Making Personalization Moves.\",\"url\":\"https://www.convert.com/blog/a-b-testing/google-ads-website-optimizer-2025/\"},{\"title\":\"Top 5 Google Cloud Cost Optimization Tools | Ternary\",\"url\":\"https://ternary.app/blog/google-cloud-cost-optimization-tools/\"},{\"title\":\"Top Google Shopping Feed Tips for Success\",\"url\":\"https://www.channable.com/blog/google-shopping-feed-optimization\"},{\"title\":\"Semrush Enterprise - The AI launchpad for elevated digital marketing\",\"url\":\"https://enterprise.semrush.com/solutions/ai-optimization/\"},{\"title\":\"World's leading AI-powered digital experiences - Optimizely\",\"url\":\"https://www.optimizely.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization tips for Performance Max campaign for all business types - Google Ads Help\",\"url\":\"https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/11385582?hl=en\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found that the query didn't return information specifically about Google OR-Tools with customer testimonials about production optimization. The search results primarily returned content about:\n\n1. **Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) agencies** - marketing agencies optimizing for AI search\n2. **Google Cloud cost optimization tools** - GCP FinOps platforms\n3. **Google Ads optimization** - Performance Max campaigns and advertising optimization\n4. **E-commerce optimization** - Google Shopping feed optimization\n\nNone of the search results contained customer testimonials or case studies specifically about Google OR-Tools being used in production optimization environments. Google OR-Tools is Google's open-source operations research library for solving optimization and scheduling problems, but the search results didn't return relevant information about its customer adoption or testimonials.\n\nTo find customer testimonials about Google OR-Tools for production optimization, you might want to:\n- Check the official Google OR-Tools documentation and case studies on their GitHub repository or Google Cloud website\n- Search for \"Google OR-Tools case studies\" or \"OR-Tools customer success\"\n- Look at Google Cloud's success stories page\n\nWould you like me to perform a different search with alternative keywords to find information about Google OR-Tools usage?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b1a5655a-c598-4519-8507-c9caa2f59ccd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:47.478Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"46e6c4d1-a867-466c-8a39-3de02fc550d1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1d482103-d6d9-4655-b1e3-ee43322f2613","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0da025bf-5462-4d88-9ddf-73d39057a5ff","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N23mebkECeM8ukGxyaaovc","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"CP-SAT\" 70x70 OR \"large grid\" OR \"168 hours\" OR \"long running\" exact proof optimization production\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization of Timed Petri Nets using CP-SAT - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2405896324000946\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"A practical introduction to Constraint Programming using CP-SAT and Python\",\"url\":\"https://pganalyze.com/blog/a-practical-introduction-to-constraint-programming-using-cp-sat\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Rostering: Complete Guide to Constraint Programming for Workforce Scheduling - Interactive | Michael Brenndoerfer | Michael Brenndoerfer\",\"url\":\"https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/cp-sat-rostering-constraint-programming-workforce-scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"Solver Max - CP-SAT primer\",\"url\":\"https://www.solvermax.com/resources/links/blogs-about-optimization/cp-sat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"Solver Max - Well, that escalated quickly: OR-Tools\",\"url\":\"https://www.solvermax.com/blog/well-that-escalated-quickly-or-tools\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query. The results show information about CP-SAT, which is a solver designed for integer programming problems that is generally faster than MPSolver. \n\nThe search results include:\n\n1. **Google's CP-SAT Solver documentation** - Official OR-Tools documentation about the solver\n2. **CP-SAT Primer** - A comprehensive guide for using and understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\n3. **Academic and practical applications** - Including papers on optimizing Timed Petri Nets with CP-SAT and constraint programming for workforce scheduling\n4. **Performance analysis** - Discussion of CP-SAT's capability to find good solutions quickly, with optimization proofs achieved for most data sets within 1 hour of run time\n\nHowever, the search results don't specifically mention the \"70x70\" grid size, \"168 hours,\" or \"long running exact proof optimization production\" scenarios you were looking for. The results focus more on general CP-SAT capabilities and applications rather than these specific parameters. If you're looking for more targeted information about large grid optimization problems with CP-SAT or specific production use cases, you may want to refine your search or provide additional context.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ff9e02a0-5eee-4579-a290-382bc4dcef6f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:47.656Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1d482103-d6d9-4655-b1e3-ee43322f2613","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a866d378-4275-414a-9925-512f172326ed","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0da025bf-5462-4d88-9ddf-73d39057a5ff","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011UhpswGPjHqfyFismpKRE5","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Hexaly\" OR \"LocalSolver\" CP-SAT comparison industrial customers warehouse layout\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Now we are Hexaly\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/announcements/now-we-are-hexaly\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/\"},{\"title\":\"LocalSolver 7.0 — Hexaly 14.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/changelog/localsolver70.html\"},{\"title\":\"LocalSolver (LocalSolver 8.0 API)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/8_0/java/localsolver/LocalSolver.html\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly, CP Optimizer, OR-Tools, Gurobi, Cplex on very large-scale instances of the Job Shop Scheduling Problem (JSSP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks/hexaly-vs-cp-optimizer-vs-or-tools-on-the-job-shop-scheduling-problem-jssp\"},{\"title\":\"LocalSolver (LocalSolver 12.5 API)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/12_5/java/localsolver/LocalSolver.html\"},{\"title\":\"Localsolver: Package localsolver\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/6_0/csharp/namespacelocalsolver.html\"},{\"title\":\"LocalSolver (LocalSolver 6.0 API)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/6_0/java/localsolver/LocalSolver.html\"},{\"title\":\"Migrate from LocalSolver to Hexaly — Hexaly 14.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/changelog/migration.html\"},{\"title\":\"Solvers for Scheduling and Routing Problems |\",\"url\":\"https://dmcommunity.org/2024/04/16/localsolver-is-now-hexaly/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about Hexaly (formerly LocalSolver) and its capabilities related to warehouse layout optimization. Here's what I found:\n\n## Hexaly and Warehouse Layout Optimization\n\nHexaly Optimizer identifies Warehouse Layout and Picking Optimization as one of its areas of specialization, claiming to be the best solver available in the market for these problems.\n\n## Relationship Between Hexaly and LocalSolver\n\nLocalSolver transitioned to the new brand identity Hexaly. Since November 2023, LocalSolver has become Hexaly, with this new name intended to better reflect the solver's evolution from one based on local search techniques to a global optimization solver combining numerous optimization techniques.\n\n## Comparison with CP-SAT\n\nThe search results do show that Hexaly has been compared with other optimization solvers including Google OR-Tools CP-SAT in benchmarks. However, the search results provided don't contain specific information about:\n\n- Direct comparisons between Hexaly/LocalSolver and CP-SAT specifically on warehouse layout problems\n- Information about industrial customers using these solvers for warehouse layout optimization\n\nThe results focus mainly on job shop scheduling benchmarks rather than warehouse layout applications. For more specific information about industrial customer case studies or detailed warehouse layout comparisons between these solvers, you may need to search the Hexaly benchmarks page directly or contact the vendor.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2479015f-6fa8-4691-9806-5fc2650d12a6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:49.394Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a866d378-4275-414a-9925-512f172326ed","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"932cb3e3-bc29-4da1-9857-5569f7f64f3d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0da025bf-5462-4d88-9ddf-73d39057a5ff","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Akg5Phy4bcgfQSgPPG6gwg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"CP-SAT\" steel cutting glass cutting 2D guillotine industrial optimization deployed\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A simple approach to the two-dimensional guillotine cutting stock problem | Journal of Industrial Engineering International\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/2251-712X-8-21\"},{\"title\":\"Guillotine cutting - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guillotine_cutting\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A Genetic Algorithm for 2D Glass Cutting Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/228691239_A_Genetic_Algorithm_for_2D_Glass_Cutting_Problem\"},{\"title\":\"A Constraint Programming Solution to the Guillotine Rectangular Cutting Problem\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/ICAPS/article/download/27213/26986\"},{\"title\":\"An optimization algorithm for cutting stock problems in the TFT-LCD industry - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0360835209000928\"},{\"title\":\"A Constraint Programming Solution to the Guillotine Rectangular Cutting Problem\",\"url\":\"https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/papers/guillotine-pack.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Two-stage two-dimensional guillotine cutting stock problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.ime.usp.br/~egbirgin/publications/abmro.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Cutting stock problem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cutting_stock_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Two-stage and one-group two-dimensional guillotine cutting problems with defects: a CP-based algorithm and ILP formulations: International Journal of Production Research: Vol 60 , No 6 - Get Access\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00207543.2021.1876270\"},{\"title\":\"Cut 2D X - wood, glass, metal, sheet, paper, cutting and nesting library\",\"url\":\"https://www.optimalprograms.com/cut_2d_x.htm\"}]\n\nI found search results related to 2D guillotine cutting problems for steel and glass cutting with industrial optimization. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Industrial Applications**: Guillotine cutting is particularly common in the glass industry, where glass sheets are scored along horizontal and vertical lines and broken to obtain smaller panels. It is also useful for cutting steel plates, cutting of wood sheets to make furniture, and cutting of cardboard into boxes.\n\n**Constraint Programming Approaches**: The search results reveal that constraint programming (CP) has been successfully applied to 2D guillotine cutting problems. Google OR-Tools CP-SAT Solver is referenced in academic literature on guillotine cutting optimization.\n\n**Real-World Problem Variants**: Different manufacturing settings cut defective objects, with real-world applications including the production of flat glass in the glass industry and the cutting of wooden boards with knotholes in the furniture industry.\n\n**Computational Methods**: Constraint Programming (CP) based algorithms as well as Integer Linear Programming (ILP) formulations have been proposed to solve these problems effectively.\n\nThe search results show that CP-SAT and similar constraint programming approaches are used in academic research for optimizing 2D guillotine cutting problems in industrial settings, particularly for glass and steel cutting applications.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c830da3b-5e77-4be0-91ed-c643410fe32d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:49.590Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"932cb3e3-bc29-4da1-9857-5569f7f64f3d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":