{"parentUuid":"81d1f091-b632-4ed0-99d6-648e32d91774","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0da025bf-5462-4d88-9ddf-73d39057a5ff","agentId":"a43e97232d861bfd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N5XsoQZWfqH38ESCf9n59L","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools-discuss\" \"production\" deployment experience large model timeout\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OpenAI model deployment timeout issues - Microsoft Q&A\",\"url\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/answers/questions/5491225/openai-model-deployment-timeout-issues\"},{\"title\":\"How to troubleshoot your deployments and monitors in Microsoft Foundry portal (classic) - Microsoft Foundry (classic) portal | Microsoft Learn\",\"url\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry-classic/how-to/troubleshoot-deploy-and-monitor\"},{\"title\":\"Router - Load Balancing | liteLLM\",\"url\":\"https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/routing\"},{\"title\":\"Challenges in Deploying Machine Learning: A Survey of Case Studies | ACM Computing Surveys\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/full/10.1145/3533378\"},{\"title\":\"AI model deployment: Best practices for production environments | LaunchDarkly\",\"url\":\"https://launchdarkly.com/blog/ai-model-deployment/\"},{\"title\":\"Debug model serving timeouts | Databricks on AWS\",\"url\":\"https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/machine-learning/model-serving/model-serving-timeouts\"},{\"title\":\"Deploying AI Models to Production in the Cloud\",\"url\":\"https://www.infracloud.io/blogs/deploying-ai-models-to-production-in-cloud/\"},{\"title\":\"How would you design the system architecture for deploying a large language model (LLM) in production?\",\"url\":\"https://www.designgurus.io/answers/detail/how-would-you-design-the-system-architecture-for-deploying-a-large-language-model-llm-in-production\"},{\"title\":\"Considerations for Deploying Machine Learning Models in Production\",\"url\":\"https://www.anyscale.com/blog/considerations-for-deploying-machine-learning-models-in-production\"},{\"title\":\"Debug model serving timeouts - Azure Databricks | Microsoft Learn\",\"url\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/databricks/machine-learning/model-serving/model-serving-timeouts\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information related to production deployment experiences with large model timeout issues, though the results don't specifically focus on \"or-tools-discuss\" discussions. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## Key Findings on Production Deployment and Timeout Issues:\n\nCommercial LLM APIs have latencies of 5–30 seconds for complex queries, so expectations and timeouts should be set accordingly.\n\n### Timeout Issues in Model Deployment:\n\nModel deployment timeouts vary by workload type: up to 30 minutes for CPU workloads, 60 minutes for GPU small or medium workloads, and 120 minutes for GPU large workloads.\n\nCold start latency can affect performance, especially with larger models.\n\n### Production Challenges:\n\nA common problem with currently available end-to-end ML platforms is that final ML solutions are usually so sensitive to a problem's specifics that out-of-the-box tooling does not fit their needs well.\n\nSensible timeouts should be set up so users aren't left hanging too long on a bad request.\n\n### Solutions:\n\nBasic reliability logic includes cooldowns, fallbacks, timeouts and retries (fixed + exponential backoff) across multiple deployments/providers.\n\nThe search results provide general guidance on managing large model deployments and timeout issues in production environments, but do not contain specific discussions from the \"or-tools-discuss\" forum mentioned in your query.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8b7f8b10-4771-4e9e-a18f-81dd0f92dc4a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:12:10.250Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"81d1f091-b632-4ed0-99d6-648e32d91774","userType":"external","en