results, I found comprehensive information about Satalia and \"Decision Brain\" (referred to as \"audience brains\" in the results). Here's what I discovered:\n\n## Satalia Overview\n\nSatalia delivers AI-powered solutions for optimising complex operational processes and decision-making in organisations. The company name Satalia is a portmanteau of SAT (Short for satisfiability, as in the Boolean satisfiability problem) and the Latin phrase Et alia.\n\n## Decision Brain / Audience Brains\n\nSatalia is creating an audience representation of a human being through what they call \"audience brains.\" Founder Daniel Hulme, whose company was acquired by WPP in 2021, has been working to \"glue\" these brains to generative AI such as ChatGPT in order to make campaign assets based specifically on brand data.\n\n## Industrial/Corporate Clients\n\nSatalia provides AI products and consultancy for governments and companies such as Tesco, DFS Furniture, PwC and the BBC. Satalia's first major breakthrough around 2014 was with Tesco, which had a large-scale optimisation problem for delivering groceries to customers, eventually commissioning Satalia to build their entire 'last mile' delivery solution.\n\n## CP-SAT and Kepler\n\nThe search results did not contain specific information about \"CP-SAT\" or \"Kepler\" in relation to Satalia's consulting services. You may want to search more specifically for these terms if you need additional information about those particular aspects.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9e5accb1-cdaa-479a-8feb-f576d8aa0bfc","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:12:11.236Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"46705649-9c21-466e-8d72-049e3daa0130","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
